w marilyn have you  characterized the expression  profile of these il-10 producing b  cells and based on unsupervised  clustering do these il t  10 plus b cells cluster together as well  uh yeah that would be very interesting  so there are studies from peripheral  blood where  you can kind of capture the il-10 on the  outside of the cell  and then they um earlier studies did  some  sorting of these cells and also then  some analysis but unfortunately these  um cells we have now alpha and producing  b cells  are so few again that we we couldn't do  that for now  um but in a future single cell analysis  that would be interesting to  uh yeah really select only these il-10  producing cells and then  yeah study them in more detail  now are the b cells present in the  placenta  fetal or maternal and is there  immunogenic learning going on  within the uterus um  okay so two questions b cells present  and the placenta feta are maternal  so we uh right now only isolates the  maternal tissues so we consider what  is a continuum kind of from menstrual  blood endometrium samples  uh through first and second trimester we  um  we selected mucosal tissue that we then  i think is tissue from the mother and  especially with the um  first and second trimester samples um i  don't think at that point there's  um or does sorry  the fetal membranes didn't fuse with the  maternal membranes yet so  whatever we have at that point uh is  really maternal  and also for term samples we do select  only the citral parietals so the  maternal  layer of the placenta um  is there immunogenic learning  i think that's um that's an interesting  point and that also our group focuses on  especially now for nk self and um  yeah we we didn't look at that for for  business until now so it would be  interesting to then  uh follow up um b cells maybe from  menstrual blood samples of  women who have been pregnant and then  later on check if their b-cell profile  is different because they have been  pregnant bef